2. Python Code to Read and Calculate Averages
import pandas as pd

# Read the dataset
df = pd.read_csv("sample_weather.txt")

# Display first few rows
print(df.head())

# Calculate averages
avg_temp = df['Temperature'].mean()
avg_dew = df['DewPoint'].mean()
avg_wind = df['WindSpeed'].mean()

# Print results
print("Average Temperature:", avg_temp)
print("Average Dew Point:", avg_dew)
print("Average Wind Speed:", avg_wind)




Explanation
pd.read_csv() → reads the text file into a DataFrame
.mean() → calculates the average of a column
Columns used:
Temperature
DewPoint
WindSpeed

